  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "47122c6e-d678-4824-bbee-0349ede3bc27",
    "name": "Eat App Platform Concierge - Availability Concierge - Guests API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "Eat App is a restaurant reservation and table management platform. This document models its two documented, partner/key-gated REST surfaces plus a small honestly-modeled table-management surface:\n1. Partner API (base /partners/v2) - for booking channels to read availability and post reservations.\n2. Concierge API (base /concierge/v2) - for restaurants, vendors, and groups to sync reservations, guests, availability, and reference data (resources, groups, restaurants). Requests are scoped with X-Group-ID and X-Restaurant-ID headers and can be created idempotently via an idempotency_token.\n3. Tables and Floor Plans (base /concierge/v2) - MODELED. No public tables or floorplan endpoints are documented; these operations are honestly modeled on Eat App's documented resource conventions and should be confirmed with a partner API key before use.\nAll responses follow a JSON:API-style structure (data objects carrying id, type, and attributes). Every request is authenticated with a Bearer token (the API key Eat App issues to a partner or Concierge user). The sandbox host is https://api.eat-sandbox.co and production is https://api.eatapp.co. Endpoints are rate limited to roughly 60 requests per minute.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Eat App",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
